+## File uploads and recorder input
+
+Use `transcriptionFile(file)` to retain a File's name and MIME type with OpenAI or Groq. Supply `{ mediaType, filename }` to override either label. For a Blob without a type or a byte stream, provide the MIME type. An unnamed byte array can also use an existing byte-only adapter with its explicit MIME. A replayable File supports normal retries. A one-shot byte stream requires a fetch implementation that supports request streaming, and gets one attempt.
+
+OpenAI file models such as `gpt-4o-mini-transcribe` accept a recording and send transcript deltas over HTTP. Pass `audio: transcriptionFile(file)` to `experimental_streamTranscribe` and consume `fullStream` before reading the authoritative `text` from the same result. Diarized `transcript-final` events carry the speaker in provider metadata.
+
+Deepgram Nova and Flux accept ordered WebM/Opus, Ogg/Opus or WAV/linear16 chunks from a single recorder. Pass its byte stream as `audio` and its MIME as `inputAudioFormat.type`. Omit the rate for a container. Set `providerOptions.deepgram.streaming.interimResults` for Nova interim text. Flux revises the current turn until it ends. On normal input shutdown it drains the last update before completing.
+
+One-shot uploads require a fetch transport that streams HTTP request bodies. In a browser without that capability, supply a completed Blob or File. Compatible browser transports can also require HTTPS over HTTP/2 or later. Live recorder transcription uses a WebSocket.
+
